<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <record id="view_dvz_policy_setup_wizard_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">dvz.policy.setup.wizard.form</field><field name="model">dvz.policy.setup.wizard</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form string="Set Up One Employee">
                <field name="policy_state" invisible="1"/>
                <div class="alert alert-info" role="alert" invisible="setup_applied">Select one existing employee. Apply activates an unused draft or uses a compatible active policy and assigns it to this employee. Joining and probation dates may remain empty when they are not yet confirmed. Allocation is a separate optional step.</div>
                <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert" invisible="not setup_applied">The policy is assigned to the employee shown below. Paid leave eligibility and allocations are checked separately.</div>
                <div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert" invisible="joining_date and employment_status == 'permanent' and (paid_eligible_date or probation_end_date)">Policy assignment is available now. Paid leave and an annual allocation require confirmed permanent status, the verified joining date, and a first paid leave date or recorded probation end. No probation duration is assumed.</div>
                <group>
                    <group string="Selected Employee">
                        <field name="company_id" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                        <field name="employee_id" options="{'no_create': True}" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                        <field name="employment_status" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                        <field name="joining_date" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                        <field name="probation_end_date" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                        <field name="paid_eligible_date" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                    </group>
                    <group string="Actual Approvers">
                        <field name="hod_user_id" options="{'no_create': True}" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                        <field name="hr_user_id" options="{'no_create': True}" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                        <field name="management_user_id" options="{'no_create': True}" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                        <field name="setup_applied" readonly="1"/>
                    </group>
                </group>
                <notebook>
                    <page string="Policy and Types" name="setup_policy">
                        <group>
                            <group>
                                <field name="policy_id" options="{'no_create': True}" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                                <field name="name" readonly="setup_applied or policy_state == 'active'"/>
                                <field name="date_from" readonly="setup_applied or policy_state == 'active'"/>
                                <field name="date_to" readonly="setup_applied or policy_state == 'active'"/>
                                <field name="result_policy_id" readonly="1" invisible="not result_policy_id"/>
                            </group>
                            <group>
                                <field name="annual_leave_type_id" options="{'no_create': True}" readonly="setup_applied or policy_state == 'active'"/>
                                <field name="unpaid_leave_type_id" options="{'no_create': True}" readonly="setup_applied or policy_state == 'active'"/>
                                <field name="wfh_leave_type_id" options="{'no_create': True}" readonly="setup_applied or policy_state == 'active'"/>
                            </group>
                        </group>
                        <p class="text-muted">Blank type selections create dedicated types for a draft. Existing types are reused only when already compatible; they are never reconfigured. Active policy rules, dates, types and approval routes remain unchanged.</p>
                    </page>
                    <page string="Automatic Employee Check" name="auto_employee_check">
                        <div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">Run the check after selecting one employee. It refreshes the fields from saved employee details and the current Odoo employment record, subject to your HR access. Unsaved candidates are replaced. Contract start is shown as a reference, not as the original joining date. Review the dates and approvers that are known; missing eligibility dates do not prevent assignment.</div>
                        <button name="action_auto_check_employee" type="object" string="Check Employee and Probation Dates" class="btn-primary" invisible="setup_applied"/>
                        <group>
                            <field name="auto_checked_employee_id" readonly="1"/>
                            <field name="auto_contract_start" readonly="1"/>
                            <field name="auto_probation_end" readonly="1"/>
                            <field name="auto_paid_date" readonly="1"/>
                        </group>
                        <field name="auto_check_notes" readonly="1" nolabel="1"/>
                    </page>
                    <page string="Review" name="setup_review">
                        <p>The shared policy provides 24 working days per calendar year, prorating new joiners, HOD/HR approvals, one calendar day's half-day notice, WFH responsibilities, verified LWP, Management exceptions and year-end encashment.</p>
                        <p>The source does not state the exact proration/rounding method, full-day or WFH notice duration, or salary rate. Review those choices on the draft. Rates are entered on the settlement, with no payroll posting.</p>
                        <p>Review the employee details that are known. Leave unconfirmed eligibility dates empty; HR can complete them later on the employee's Leave Policy tab before paid leave is granted.</p>
                        <field name="reviewed" readonly="setup_applied"/>
                    </page>
                    <page string="Optional Employee Allocation" name="setup_allocation" invisible="not setup_applied">
                        <group>
                            <group>
                                <field name="as_of_date"/>
                                <field name="allocation_status" readonly="1"/>
                                <field name="allocation_days" readonly="1"/>
                            </group>
                            <group>
                                <field name="allocation_period_start" readonly="1"/>
                                <field name="allocation_period_end" readonly="1"/>
                                <field name="allocation_id" readonly="1"/>
                            </group>
                        </group>
                        <field name="allocation_message" readonly="1" nolabel="1"/>
                        <p class="text-muted">Preview checks only this employee. Existing unreviewed paid allocations prevent a new grant. Repeated generation reuses the same grant and leaves approval to the normal allocation workflow.</p>
                    </page>
                </notebook>
                <footer>
                    <button name="action_auto_check_employee" string="Auto-Check Employee" type="object" invisible="setup_applied"/>
                    <button name="action_create_draft" string="Save Policy Draft" type="object" invisible="setup_applied or policy_state == 'active'"/>
                    <button name="action_apply_employee" string="Apply to This Employee" type="object" class="btn-primary" invisible="setup_applied"/>
                    <button name="action_preview_allocation" string="Preview Employee Allocation" type="object" class="btn-primary" invisible="not setup_applied"/>
                    <button name="action_generate_allocation" string="Generate Employee Allocation" type="object" invisible="not setup_applied or allocation_status not in ('create','reuse')"/>
                    <button string="Close" special="cancel" class="btn-secondary"/>
                </footer>
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>
    <record id="action_dvz_policy_setup_wizard" model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Set Up One Employee</field><field name="res_model">dvz.policy.setup.wizard</field>
        <field name="view_mode">form</field><field name="target">new</field>
    </record>
</odoo>
